 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 22%).","At current returns, reinvesting 52% of profits supports about 11.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 1.1% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 62%.","Capex runs 2.0x depreciation (17.3% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 17, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and institutions hold 89%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $8.4M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.5% (0.2% in buybacks and 1.3% in dividends)."],"people":["With about 29,000 employees, each generates about $894K of revenue, 1.4x the Basic Materials median.","That works out to $38K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.0M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":64,"head":"Avoid: priced 358% above its fair value of $10.05.","pros":["Composite 48, above the 39 line (gates 12/26)","ROIC 21.4% vs WACC 10.9%","Revenue grew 12.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.6x","22 analysts' mean target $78.22 (+70%)"],"cons":["Trades 358% above fair value of $10.05","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 19.3x vs sector 14.2x","P/FCF 59.1x vs sector 20.4x"],"flags":["Priced 358% above its fair value of $10.05"],"need":[],"buy_below":8.54,"vc":{"base":10.05,"base_src":"dcf","bear":5.87,"bull":18.34,"alt_median":11.41,"n_alt":3,"gap":-0.0388,"dispersion":0.1478,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","bull case is 3.1x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":14.1531,"ev_ebitda":7.701,"pfcf":20.3799,"pb":1.7565,"roic":0.0589,"gross_margin":0.2564,"fcf_margin":0.052,"div_yield":0.0205}},"mc_quantiles":[3.66,4.99,5.87,6.54,7.1